From 43433122a9177c7a5bd348eca75f4f38e1389fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:41:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/49] trap-screenshot: -trap-screenshot +

The SHOT handler first landed in coco3.c with the instruction_shot
delegate wired for that machine only.  The core decodes the LOG command
for every 6809 machine and DELEGATE_SAFE_CALL swallows a call through an
unwired delegate, so a Dragon-family guest requesting SHOT got no file
and no warning -- the worst kind of no.  Nothing in the handler ever
touched machine state (its sptr was unused), so it moves to debug.c
beside the other shared emuext bodies, and both 6809 machine families
wire the delegate through the same thin trampoline shape emuext_log
already uses.
---
